# ============================================================
# AVS-OPS-001 (2026-09-04) — pre-commit-1 additions.
# Section 3 of the prompt permits one .gitignore edit before commit 3 to keep
# bulk out of the baseline commit. Verified NOT ignored at that point:
#   backups/        59 dirs, 14,518 files, 35.0 GB (5 files >100 MB)
#   data/canonical/ 6,261 stageable files, 463 MB of canonical dataset payloads
#   .codex_*/       vendored CPython runtimes, 5,849 files, 103.6 MB
#                   (ACK decision 2026-09-04: ignore rather than commit-then-attic,
#                    so the runtime never enters permanent history)
# data/ is NOT excluded wholesale: that would defeat the
# !data/universe/polygon_liquid_universe.csv negation above and untrack the
# 5 files already tracked under data/. The 9 files already tracked under
# backups/ are unaffected — .gitignore does not untrack.
# ============================================================
backups/
data/canonical/
.codex_*/

# ============================================================
# AVS-OPS-001 (2026-09-04) — commit 3. Scratch, cache and backup patterns so
# root debris stops coming back. Only patterns absent from the rules above are
# added; __pycache__/, .pytest_cache/, pytest-of-*/, *.bak, *.bak_*, .env,
# .env.txt, *.lnk and .codex_*/ were already present.
#
# These are ANCHORED to the repository root with a leading slash. The unanchored
# forms in the AVS-OPS-001 prompt would have over-matched tracked evidence:
#   tmp*/        -> audit/olm_fix_test/tmp_runs/ and
#                   audit/pipeline_map/AVS-TST-SD-002-001/tmp/ (tracked test XMLs)
#   *old0908.py  -> _attic/bond_macro_intelligenceold0908.py and
#                   _attic/build_macro_jsonold0908.py, which must stay tracked
# Verified: each anchored pattern matches 0 tracked paths.
#
# _attic/ is deliberately NOT ignored — it must stay tracked so every move in
# commit 4c33c1c is visible and reversible with a single git mv back.
# ============================================================
/tmp*/
/pip-*/
/avs_macro_check_*/
/*old0908.py
*.rr_cap.bak

# ============================================================
# AVS-FIX-001 W0.1 (2026-09-06) — baseline commit. `git add -A` aborted with
#   error: open("audit/ddd_closure_testdeps/py.py"): Permission denied
# These are pytest basetemp / vendored-testdep scratch trees left by the DDD
# closure and SD-002 remediation runs. Windows left restrictive ACLs on them,
# so git cannot read them at all — they can never be committed, and they are
# the same "ephemeral test scratch" class as the pytest-of-*/ rule above.
#
# ANCHORED to the repository root, and each verified to match 0 tracked paths:
#   audit/pipeline_map/AVS-TST-SD-002-001/ holds 71 tracked files, 9 of them
#   XMLs directly inside tmp/codex_remediation/ — so only that directory's
#   SUBDIRECTORIES (the pytest basetemps) are excluded, never the XMLs.
#   audit/pipeline_logic_review/ holds 3 tracked design notes — only its
#   pytest_tmp_ws2*/ scratch is excluded.
#   audit/olm_fix_test/tmp_runs/ is deliberately NOT listed: it is tracked
#   evidence (see the AVS-OPS-001 note above).
# ============================================================
/audit/ddd_closure_full_tmp_20260905/
/audit/ddd_closure_testdeps/
/audit/ddd_closure_tmp_20260905/
/audit/ddd_isolated_release_tmp_20260905/
/audit/ddd_isolated_tmp_20260905/
/audit/ddd_msi_w20_tmp_20260905/
/audit/ddd_readiness_tmp/
/audit/ddd_runtime_profile_tmp_20260905/
/audit/ddd_test_tmp/
/audit/ddd_test_tmp_full/
/audit/pipeline_logic_review/pytest_tmp_ws2*/
/audit/pipeline_map/.design_validation_tmp/
/audit/pipeline_map/AVS-TST-SD-002-001/tmp/codex_remediation/*/

# ============================================================
# AVS-FIX-001 W0.4 (2026-09-06). The blanket *.csv rule above also swallows
# audit EVIDENCE — AVS-TST-QT-001's own B_<run>.csv gate tables are untracked
# for this reason. A register that is not in the repository cannot be cited by
# a commit or reviewed in a diff, so the AVS-IMP-FIX-001 evidence directory is
# negated. Scoped to that one directory: run outputs elsewhere stay ignored,
# and these files are small, hand-reviewable classification tables, not data.
# ============================================================
!audit/pipeline_map/AVS-IMP-FIX-001/*.csv
